      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "Elon Musk explains why Tesla is being extremely careful while scaling Robotaxi\n\nThe ambition is massive...but Elon’s priority is making sure they do not hurt anyone\n\nThere are roughly 30,000–40,000 automotive deaths every year in the U.S., and most receive almost no national attention\n\nBut if a Tesla Robotaxi injures even ONE person, it can instantly become worldwide headline news and regulators could clamp down on the entire operation\n\nSo Tesla has to do two things at the same time:\n\nScale Robotaxi as fast as humanly possible\n\nAND make sure it causes essentially no harm\n\nElon put it very simply:\n\n“We do not want to injure anyone”\n\n“And ideally...not even run over a pet”\n\nThat is the real constraint on Robotaxi right now\n\nAnd despite being this cautious, the rollout is accelerating fast\n\nTesla’s authorized Cybercab fleet in Texas has nearly QUADRUPLED in just one month\n\n45 → 169 Cybercabs\n\nAnd Tesla now has 589 Robotaxi vehicles authorized in Texas when you include 420 Model Ys\n\nUnsupervised Robotaxi miles have also been growing at double-digit rates week after week\n\nSo Tesla is not moving slowly\n\nIt’s scaling incredibly fast while trying to maintain an insanely high safety bar\n\nThat’s the balance Elon is trying to solve https://x.com/XFreeze/status/2080096187584274809/video/1",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "XFreeze",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1876785200010539008/2_HFJjq9_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-04 05:25:44",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-03T21:25:44.000Z",
        "id": "2106495942019170587",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2080095935502454784/img/vJr3gzYWyx8MIzhe.jpg"
        ],
        "media": [
